      {
        "name": "fix",
        "description": "Apply the profile's mechanical replacements (fixes) and print the fixed text.\n\nDeterministic, no LLM: what to replace with what is in the profile, in\nits order. Only the text a reader sees changes — HTML text nodes (tags,\nattributes and block order stay byte for byte), md outside code; code,\npre, script, style, md code, link targets and bare URLs are never touched.\nDefault output: the fixed text on stdout, a summary on stderr. --json:\n{ok, text, applied[{name, count, addresses}], unchanged}; with --check\nalso check's {issues, humanizer, gate_failed} and its exit code.\nExit 2: bad arguments or profile (INVALID_PROFILE) — no text is printed.\n\nExample: textcheck fix article.html --profile typography.quality.yml --check --json",
        "options": [
          {
            "name": "--profile",
            "arguments": [
              {
                "name": "PROFILE",
                "required": true,
                "arity": {
                  "maximum": 1
                }
              }
            ],
            "description": "Quality profile (quality.yml) with a `fixes` section. Without fixes: text unchanged.",
            "metadata": [
